WEBVTT

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:16.221
I was at Warwick Castle in England when I met a stranger.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:20.114
He told me many stories about the past.

00:00:20.174 --> 00:00:22.726
I liked them very much.

00:00:22.786 --> 00:00:26.678
Then we saw some very old armour.

00:00:26.739 --> 00:00:30.266
There was a bullet hole in the armour.

00:00:30.326 --> 00:00:33.144
This hole is later.

00:00:33.204 --> 00:00:39.048
It comes after the invention of firearms, said the guide.

00:00:39.108 --> 00:00:45.142
I did it, said the stranger and smiled.

00:00:45.202 --> 00:00:48.154
I was very surprised.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:51.856
The stranger was staying at my hotel.

00:00:51.916 --> 00:00:57.340
He came to my room and gave me a manuscript.

00:00:57.399 --> 00:01:00.961
His name was Hank Morgan.

00:01:01.021 --> 00:01:05.132
This is his story.

00:01:05.192 --> 00:01:10.286
I was in my factory in Connecticut.

00:01:10.346 --> 00:01:15.288
A worker hit me on the head and I fell down.

00:01:15.348 --> 00:01:22.604
I woke up under a tree and saw a strange man in armour on a horse.

00:01:22.664 --> 00:01:25.835
He said I was his prisoner.

00:01:25.895 --> 00:01:29.408
His name was Sir Kay.

00:01:29.468 --> 00:01:32.360
I went with him to a village.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:36.083
He said it was Camelot.

00:01:36.142 --> 00:01:39.976
I was sure it was a lunatic asylum.

00:01:40.036 --> 00:01:43.388
I thought all the people were mad.

00:01:43.447 --> 00:01:46.710
They all looked at my clothes.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:50.703
They thought I was strange.

00:01:50.763 --> 00:01:54.516
I started to talk to a page.

00:01:54.575 --> 00:01:57.666
His name was Clarence.

00:01:57.726 --> 00:02:00.156
Where am I?

00:02:00.215 --> 00:02:01.806
I asked.

00:02:01.866 --> 00:02:07.748
King Arthur's court, in the year 513, he answered.

00:02:07.808 --> 00:02:09.909
You are a prisoner.

00:02:09.969 --> 00:02:12.340
They are going to kill you.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.632
But I will come and visit you in prison.

00:02:16.692 --> 00:02:22.654
Then some people took me to the king at his round table.

00:02:22.713 --> 00:02:27.885
There were lots of knights sitting round the table eating.

00:02:27.945 --> 00:02:31.486
Lots of people served them food.

00:02:31.546 --> 00:02:35.178
Beautiful ladies watched from a balcony.

00:02:35.237 --> 00:02:38.919
Musicians played on another balcony.

00:02:38.979 --> 00:02:43.450
The room was very big and made of stone.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:48.752
The knights’ and ladies’ clothes were beautiful.

00:02:48.812 --> 00:02:53.154
An old man stood up and told a story.

00:02:53.214 --> 00:02:57.124
Everyone was bored and fell asleep.

00:02:57.184 --> 00:03:00.794
The old man was Merlin.

00:03:00.854 --> 00:03:05.506
Then Sir Kay told the story of my capture.

00:03:05.566 --> 00:03:10.748
He told a lot of lies and said I was very dangerous.

00:03:10.808 --> 00:03:14.829
He presented me to Queen Guinevere.

00:03:14.889 --> 00:03:18.670
He said my clothes were magic.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:23.972
They took away my clothes and then put me in prison.

00:03:24.032 --> 00:03:28.076
I fell asleep.

00:03:28.136 --> 00:03:34.042
When I woke up, I thought it was all a dream.

00:03:34.102 --> 00:03:37.583
Then I realized it was true.

00:03:37.643 --> 00:03:41.884
I was a prisoner at King Arthur's Court.

00:03:41.944 --> 00:03:45.146
Clarence came to visit me.

00:03:45.206 --> 00:03:49.868
Help me to escape, I said to him.

00:03:49.927 --> 00:03:53.080
I can't, he answered.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:58.923
There are lots of guards, and Merlin has put a spell on this prison.

00:03:58.983 --> 00:04:01.064
No one can escape.

00:04:01.124 --> 00:04:05.856
Tomorrow, at noon, they are going to burn you.

00:04:05.915 --> 00:04:12.488
I was very miserable, but I had an idea.

00:04:12.548 --> 00:04:15.909
I am not afraid, I said.

00:04:15.929 --> 00:04:20.191
I am a very powerful magician.

00:04:20.251 --> 00:04:23.396
Is today the 20th of June?

00:04:23.456 --> 00:04:27.862
Yes, it is, said Clarence.

00:04:27.922 --> 00:04:36.956
Then go and tell the king that if he burns me, tomorrow the world will end in darkness.

00:04:37.016 --> 00:04:40.707
I’ll end all light and warmth.

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:42.648
Everyone will die.

00:04:42.668 --> 00:04:46.976
I knew from my studies.

00:04:47.036 --> 00:04:54.738
that on the 21st of June, 513, there was a total solar eclipse.

00:04:54.798 --> 00:05:01.113
That was my magic, to make the sun disappear.

00:05:01.173 --> 00:05:08.379
The next day, they came to get me and tied me to a big tree.

00:05:08.439 --> 00:05:12.072
People sat to watch all around.

00:05:12.132 --> 00:05:14.920
Everyone wanted to see.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.268
I was afraid.

00:05:17.328 --> 00:05:24.311
And if my calculations were wrong, then everyone looked up.

00:05:24.371 --> 00:05:27.542
The eclipse was beginning.

00:05:27.602 --> 00:05:30.084
Burn him!

00:05:30.144 --> 00:05:32.605
shouted Merlin.

00:05:32.664 --> 00:05:35.276
Stop!

00:05:35.336 --> 00:05:37.667
shouted King Arthur.

00:05:37.727 --> 00:05:40.118
Have mercy!

00:05:40.178 --> 00:05:43.099
Do not destroy the sun.

00:05:43.159 --> 00:05:44.958
What do you want?

00:05:45.018 --> 00:05:48.367
I can give you anything.

00:05:48.426 --> 00:05:54.940
I said I wanted to be his minister and help him, and he agreed.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:58.682
The solar eclipse was now total.

00:05:58.742 --> 00:06:01.264
Everything was dark.

00:06:01.323 --> 00:06:10.498
So I pointed to the sun and shouted, Pass away and do not harm us.

00:06:10.558 --> 00:06:13.921
The sun started to come out again.

00:06:13.981 --> 00:06:16.984
and everyone was happy.

00:06:17.044 --> 00:06:24.418
I became the first minister and the most powerful man in Camelot.

00:06:24.477 --> 00:06:28.170
Clarence was my assistant.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:36.554
I had beautiful but very uncomfortable clothes and the best rooms after the king.

00:06:36.614 --> 00:06:41.156
People came from all over the country to see me.

00:06:41.215 --> 00:06:43.619
I was famous.

00:06:43.679 --> 00:06:49.446
but they wanted another piece of powerful magic from me.

00:06:49.506 --> 00:06:53.199
Merlin was in prison.

00:06:53.259 --> 00:07:02.207
He was my enemy, so I said I wanted to explode his tower with fire from the sky.

00:07:02.267 --> 00:07:08.577
His tower was an old Roman one, and very solid.

00:07:08.637 --> 00:07:16.594
One stormy night, I filled it with gunpowder and attached a metal stick to it.

00:07:16.654 --> 00:07:25.896
Then I told everyone to gather, and we watched as the lightning hit the tower, and it exploded.

00:07:25.956 --> 00:07:28.717
Everyone was afraid.

00:07:28.777 --> 00:07:33.358
They thought I was a very powerful magician.

00:07:33.418 --> 00:07:39.944
As time passed, I realized that the people in Camelot were like children.

00:07:40.004 --> 00:07:42.507
They were very simple.

00:07:42.567 --> 00:07:47.438
They couldn't read or write, and they were not logical.

00:07:47.498 --> 00:07:51.679
They believed everything they heard.

00:07:51.739 --> 00:07:57.840
I started to open secret schools and a secret military academy.

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:02.011
I put down telephone wires to have telephones.

00:08:02.071 --> 00:08:05.392
I wanted to create newspapers.

00:08:05.452 --> 00:08:08.852
I taught Clarence to be a journalist.

00:08:08.912 --> 00:08:18.116
the king and the nobles believed they were better than me because I was not noble, but they respected my intelligence.

00:08:18.176 --> 00:08:25.129
I thought I was better than them because I was intelligent, but I liked them.

00:08:25.188 --> 00:08:31.451
No one admitted all this, and we got on very well.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:37.960
After four years, King Arthur was very happy with my work.

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:42.469
He was richer because I managed his money well.

00:08:42.528 --> 00:08:48.021
I also distributed it better, and the people of Camelot were happier.

00:08:48.081 --> 00:08:51.902
They started to call me the Boss.

00:08:51.962 --> 00:08:54.524
I liked it.

00:08:54.584 --> 00:08:59.736
The main entertainment at Camelot was jousting.

00:08:59.796 --> 00:09:04.364
Hundreds of knights took part, and many were injured.

00:09:04.424 --> 00:09:09.422
Sometimes the knights went to save princesses from dragons.

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:13.955
They believed in dragons and giants.

00:09:14.015 --> 00:09:18.488
One day a girl came to Camelot.

00:09:18.548 --> 00:09:22.570
Her name was Alisande la Carteloise.

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:31.270
She said her mistress and 44 girls, many of whom were princesses, were captive in a castle.

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:38.050
The guards were three huge men with four arms and one eye.

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:43.334
At Camelot, they decided I had to rescue them.

00:09:43.394 --> 00:09:49.338
I decided it was time for a holiday, so I agreed.

00:09:49.397 --> 00:09:53.171
I asked Alisande the questions.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:56.762
She couldn't tell me anything.

00:09:56.822 --> 00:09:59.612
Where is the castle?

00:09:59.672 --> 00:10:01.892
many miles away?

00:10:01.952 --> 00:10:03.532
she answered.

00:10:03.592 --> 00:10:05.014
How many?

00:10:05.074 --> 00:10:06.494
I asked.

00:10:06.554 --> 00:10:09.266
I don't know, she said.

00:10:09.326 --> 00:10:12.208
They all look the same.

00:10:12.267 --> 00:10:16.610
I got up early and had breakfast.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:19.751
Then I put on my armour.

00:10:19.811 --> 00:10:22.582
It took a very long time.

00:10:22.642 --> 00:10:27.661
There were many pieces, and I couldn't move or do anything.

00:10:27.722 --> 00:10:32.812
They had to carry me out and lift me onto the horse.

00:10:32.872 --> 00:10:36.185
I felt like a ship going to sea.

00:10:36.244 --> 00:10:40.818
Then, Alisande climbed onto the horse behind me.

00:10:40.878 --> 00:10:44.341
She had to show me the way to the castle.

00:10:44.401 --> 00:10:54.550
We started out, and everyone waved goodbye to us.

00:10:54.610 --> 00:11:03.207
We were immediately in the countryside.

00:11:03.267 --> 00:11:06.788
It was lovely and pleasant, very green.

00:11:06.848 --> 00:11:10.658
There were a lot of trees, fields, and rivers.

00:11:10.719 --> 00:11:13.619
Then it started to get hot.

00:11:13.679 --> 00:11:16.180
Sweat ran into my eyes.

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:19.900
My armour got heavier and heavier.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:28.482
Finally, Alisande took off my helmet, filled it with water, and poured it into my armour.

00:11:28.542 --> 00:11:30.764
I felt better.

00:11:30.824 --> 00:11:34.608
Alisande never stopped talking.

00:11:34.668 --> 00:11:40.570
I told her to take a rest and not use up all the air.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:43.072
Night approached.

00:11:43.132 --> 00:11:45.594
It got dark fast.

00:11:45.654 --> 00:11:51.126
I found a place for Alisande to sleep and then one for me.

00:11:51.186 --> 00:11:57.349
It got very cold and lots of insects climbed inside my armour.

00:11:57.409 --> 00:11:59.577
I couldn't sleep.

00:11:59.637 --> 00:12:05.235
In the morning I was cold, tired and hungry.

00:12:05.295 --> 00:12:11.816
Sandy was bright and fresh.

00:12:11.876 --> 00:12:16.917
We set off.

00:12:16.977 --> 00:12:22.418
Suddenly we met a group of poor, ragged people.

00:12:22.478 --> 00:12:27.289
I had breakfast with them and saw they were very happy.

00:12:27.349 --> 00:12:30.094
They were free men.

00:12:30.154 --> 00:12:36.770
they were farmers and artisans, about seven-tenths of the population.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:46.043
They were the only useful part of the population, but they could do nothing without the permission of their lords or the church.

00:12:46.103 --> 00:12:50.294
They couldn't sell anything without paying tax.

00:12:50.354 --> 00:12:57.227
They had to give part of their produce to the lords and bishops and work for them.

00:12:57.287 --> 00:13:00.158
These men were free.

00:13:00.218 --> 00:13:04.990
but they were repairing the bishops' roads as part of their duty.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:12.106
I asked them, if you had a vote tomorrow, would you vote for a king?

00:13:12.166 --> 00:13:17.469
They didn't understand, except for one man.

00:13:17.528 --> 00:13:24.713
He said, in a nation with a vote, there are no kings or bishops.

00:13:24.773 --> 00:13:29.318
I decided to send him to my man factory.

00:13:29.378 --> 00:13:34.762
A school where Clarence was teaching people to read and write.

00:13:34.822 --> 00:13:39.674
I gave the men three pennies for my breakfast.

00:13:39.734 --> 00:13:43.746
It was a lot of money, but they deserved it.

00:13:43.806 --> 00:13:47.026
Then I lit my pipe.

00:13:47.086 --> 00:13:55.614
The next day we were crossing a meadow when Sandy shouted, Defend yourself danger!

00:13:55.674 --> 00:14:00.781
Six armed knights were in the shade of a tree.

00:14:00.841 --> 00:14:03.022
They attacked me.

00:14:03.082 --> 00:14:05.802
I lit my pipe.

00:14:05.862 --> 00:14:09.113
They suddenly stopped.

00:14:09.173 --> 00:14:13.114
Sandy said they thought I was a dragon.

00:14:13.174 --> 00:14:22.505
Then she told them to go to King Arthur's court and surrender, becoming my knights.

00:14:22.565 --> 00:14:28.776
Sandy told me the story of the knights.

00:14:28.836 --> 00:14:31.308
It was very long.

00:14:31.368 --> 00:14:38.421
While she was speaking, I remembered the girl I loved in Connecticut and I was sad.

00:14:38.482 --> 00:14:42.324
But then we saw a big castle.

00:14:42.384 --> 00:14:46.456
Outside the castle I met one of my knights.

00:14:46.517 --> 00:14:49.368
He was my soap missionary.

00:14:49.428 --> 00:14:54.589
He went about selling soap because I wanted a cleaner country.

00:14:54.649 --> 00:15:01.501
He didn't manage to sell soap in that castle because someone died while they were using it.

00:15:01.561 --> 00:15:07.996
He told me the owner was Morgan Le Fay, King Arthur's sister.

00:15:08.056 --> 00:15:11.688
Her husband was King Uriens.

00:15:11.748 --> 00:15:18.532
Their kingdom was so small you could stand in the middle of it and throw a brick into the next kingdom.

00:15:18.592 --> 00:15:22.922
Morgan Le Fay had a terrible reputation.

00:15:22.982 --> 00:15:26.412
but at first she seemed very kind.

00:15:26.472 --> 00:15:29.694
She invited us to have dinner.

00:15:29.754 --> 00:15:35.316
Then a page touched her and she stabbed him.

00:15:35.376 --> 00:15:38.518
She was very bad.

00:15:38.578 --> 00:15:45.582
Sandy told her I was the Boss and she was very frightened of me.

00:15:45.642 --> 00:15:51.752
I heard a terrible sound and asked to see where it came from.

00:15:51.812 --> 00:15:57.631
As I entered the cell, I saw something I would never forget.

00:15:57.691 --> 00:16:03.216
A young giant of a man was stretched on a rack.

00:16:03.276 --> 00:16:07.630
A poor young woman with a baby was in a corner.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:12.754
The man had killed a deer, a terrible crime.

00:16:12.814 --> 00:16:18.052
I told Morgan to free him and leave me with the family.

00:16:18.112 --> 00:16:26.453
The wife wanted the man to confess, then Morgan would execute him quickly and stop his suffering.

00:16:26.513 --> 00:16:36.840
The man refused because the confession would give Morgan the right to take away all property from his wife and leave her with nothing.

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:44.275
I thought, this is a real man, a heart of gold.

00:16:44.335 --> 00:16:48.030
I asked to see her prisoners.

00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:50.374
It was terrible.

00:16:50.434 --> 00:16:54.226
Some were there so long they had gone mad.

00:16:54.286 --> 00:17:03.042
A young bride and her husband, separated by their lord on their wedding night, now didn't recognize each other.

00:17:03.102 --> 00:17:07.426
Morgan le Fay didn't even know who some of them were.

00:17:07.486 --> 00:17:11.198
An old man in his cell could see his home.

00:17:11.258 --> 00:17:14.658
He had a wife and five children.

00:17:14.718 --> 00:17:24.031
Over the years, he had seen five funerals, but he didn't know which member of his family was still alive.

00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:29.443
I set all Morgan's prisoners free except for one noble.

00:17:29.503 --> 00:17:32.855
I didn't care about him.

00:17:32.915 --> 00:17:38.458
The next morning I was very happy to leave the castle.

00:17:38.518 --> 00:17:42.040
Sandy kept telling me stories.

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:45.358
I met with my toothbrush missionary.

00:17:45.418 --> 00:17:50.150
He was very angry with my stove polish missionary.

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:59.417
Of course there were no stoves yet, but I wanted to prepare people for them and teach them about keeping a tidy home.

00:17:59.477 --> 00:18:07.554
We had another chance meeting with the old man who had watched the funerals from Morgan's prison.

00:18:07.614 --> 00:18:16.648
He was with his whole family now The funerals had been false, a torture invented by Morgan.

00:18:16.709 --> 00:18:19.740
I was happy for him.

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:23.713
Suddenly Sandy said, the castle!

00:18:23.773 --> 00:18:25.244
Look!

00:18:25.304 --> 00:18:27.996
It isn't a castle!

00:18:28.056 --> 00:18:29.996
It's a big stye!

00:18:30.056 --> 00:18:32.398
I said to Sandy.

00:18:32.458 --> 00:18:38.266
It wasn't enchanted before, she said.

00:18:38.327 --> 00:18:48.128
Sandy really believed she saw a castle with monster guards and captive princesses inside.

00:18:48.188 --> 00:18:55.872
So I paid the men who guarded the pigs to go away and rescued the ladies.

00:18:55.932 --> 00:19:02.976
Sandy embraced the pigs, believing they were princesses.

00:19:03.036 --> 00:19:07.967
The next day we met some pilgrims on the road.

00:19:08.027 --> 00:19:15.361
They were going to the valley of holiness, a place with a miraculous stream of water.

00:19:15.421 --> 00:19:22.248
Suddenly we saw a terrible sight, a group of slaves.

00:19:22.308 --> 00:19:25.570
The clothes were dirty and torn.

00:19:25.630 --> 00:19:28.332
Their faces were grey.

00:19:28.392 --> 00:19:31.656
They were injured from the chains.

00:19:31.716 --> 00:19:36.127
A girl fell, and the guards hit her.

00:19:36.187 --> 00:19:42.346
Then her new owner arrived to take her baby and her away.

00:19:42.406 --> 00:19:47.317
She cried, and a man tried to embrace her.

00:19:47.377 --> 00:19:49.537
It was her husband.

00:19:49.597 --> 00:19:51.968
They were separated.

00:19:52.028 --> 00:19:56.358
They would never see each other again.

00:19:56.418 --> 00:20:00.879
I still feel terrible when I think about that scene today.

00:20:00.899 --> 00:20:05.132
I will never forget it.

00:20:05.192 --> 00:20:10.256
We arrived at a pub where I met a knight I knew.

00:20:10.316 --> 00:20:13.688
He was my stovepipe hat missionary.

00:20:13.748 --> 00:20:17.920
He wore armour with a hat instead of a helmet.

00:20:17.981 --> 00:20:22.484
He said there was a terrible problem in the valley of holiness.

00:20:22.544 --> 00:20:24.796
The water had stopped.

00:20:24.856 --> 00:20:27.388
Merlin was there now.

00:20:27.448 --> 00:20:31.551
He was trying to make the water come back with magic.

00:20:31.611 --> 00:20:41.908
I sent a message to Clarence, send me pipes, extensions, and two trained assistants.

00:20:41.968 --> 00:20:56.797
Chapter 3. The Holy Fountain. We travelled quickly with the pilgrims and arrived in the Valley of Holiness before sunset.

00:20:56.857 --> 00:20:59.899
All the people there were sad.

00:20:59.959 --> 00:21:02.539
I met the Abbot.

00:21:02.599 --> 00:21:10.744
My son, he said, save our valley, or we will lose 200 years of work.

00:21:10.804 --> 00:21:15.058
But do not use the devil's magic.

00:21:15.118 --> 00:21:18.710
I only use God's work, I said.

00:21:18.770 --> 00:21:21.092
But what about Merlin?

00:21:21.152 --> 00:21:29.048
He promised to, but please, try immediately, answered the abbot.

00:21:29.108 --> 00:21:31.850
I can't, I said.

00:21:31.910 --> 00:21:33.550
It is not fair.

00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:37.032
I must wait until Merlin stops.

00:21:37.092 --> 00:21:40.032
I asked to see the well.

00:21:40.092 --> 00:21:45.324
I made an inspection and realized that the well probably had a leak.

00:21:45.384 --> 00:21:50.525
I went down the well and saw there was a big hole at the bottom.

00:21:50.585 --> 00:21:56.336
That was the problem, but I had to wait for Merlin to stop.

00:21:56.396 --> 00:22:01.316
The next day I decided to visit some hermits.

00:22:01.376 --> 00:22:05.766
They were all very dirty and very strange.

00:22:05.826 --> 00:22:07.897
One had chains.

00:22:07.957 --> 00:22:11.460
One was naked and black with dirt.

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:15.732
One stood on a pillar and moved up and down.

00:22:15.792 --> 00:22:21.656
Eventually I attached a sewing machine to him and made shirts.

00:22:21.716 --> 00:22:24.798
It made a lot of money.

00:22:24.858 --> 00:22:28.920
Soon Merlin decided to give in.

00:22:28.980 --> 00:22:33.702
So with my assistance I repaired the well and put in a pump.

00:22:33.762 --> 00:22:38.524
Then we made a tunnel for the water to flow outside too.

00:22:38.585 --> 00:22:41.626
I put down some fireworks.

00:22:41.686 --> 00:22:46.000
I called everyone and started the miracle.

00:22:46.060 --> 00:22:51.923
I said very big, strange, invented words.

00:22:51.984 --> 00:22:55.170
Everyone thought they were magic.

00:22:55.230 --> 00:23:01.037
Then I lit the fireworks and the water started to flow.

00:23:01.097 --> 00:23:05.028
It was a huge miracle.

00:23:05.088 --> 00:23:10.041
Soon after I asked if the monks wanted a bath.

00:23:10.101 --> 00:23:12.392
They were horrified.

00:23:12.452 --> 00:23:18.594
Baths were forbidden because people having baths stopped the water in the past.

00:23:18.654 --> 00:23:24.440
But I told them it was a different problem that stopped the water, not the bath.

00:23:24.500 --> 00:23:32.344
they were very happy and loved the swimming pool I built for them to wash in.

00:23:32.404 --> 00:23:39.125
One day I was walking in the valley when I heard a voice in a cave.

00:23:39.186 --> 00:23:42.756
It was one of my telephone operators.

00:23:42.816 --> 00:23:50.882
I asked to speak to Camelot and learnt that the king and the court were coming to visit the valley.

00:23:50.942 --> 00:24:01.221
When I returned to the monastery, I had a horrible surprise, a new giant magician.

00:24:01.282 --> 00:24:09.776
He said he knew what everyone was doing, the Emperor of the East, the Supreme Lord of India and others.

00:24:09.836 --> 00:24:13.758
Everyone believed him and was very surprised.

00:24:13.818 --> 00:24:19.141
I asked, what is my right hand doing?

00:24:19.201 --> 00:24:21.423
He didn't know.

00:24:21.482 --> 00:24:24.004
He was very worried.

00:24:24.064 --> 00:24:28.648
No one had ever asked that sort of simple question before.

00:24:28.708 --> 00:24:33.771
Then I asked, what is the king doing?

00:24:33.831 --> 00:24:38.824
He answered, he is sleeping in the palace.

00:24:38.884 --> 00:24:44.618
Everyone was amazed, but I answered, he isn't.

00:24:44.678 --> 00:24:46.620
He is traveling by horse.

00:24:46.680 --> 00:24:50.257
He will be here in three days.

00:24:50.317 --> 00:25:00.338
No one believed me, but I checked every day with my telephone operators and when the king was arriving I announced this to the abbot.

00:25:00.398 --> 00:25:07.082
People immediately stopped believing the false magician and believed me again.

00:25:07.142 --> 00:25:20.936
It is not difficult to be a successful magician in King Arthur's time, but it is hard work, and you can't rest.

00:25:20.996 --> 00:25:28.614
When the king arrived, he told me about his new army.

00:25:28.674 --> 00:25:30.945
I was not happy.

00:25:31.005 --> 00:25:36.426
I had a military school, and I wanted to make my students officers.

00:25:36.486 --> 00:25:42.768
But when we had an examination of the candidates, the nobles did not accept my men.

00:25:42.828 --> 00:25:47.700
They only accepted other nobles, who were stupid and ignorant.

00:25:47.760 --> 00:25:53.614
My men were very well prepared, but they were not noble.

00:25:53.674 --> 00:25:59.302
Another problem with these people and their strange ideas.

00:25:59.362 --> 00:26:02.034
I had another idea.

00:26:02.094 --> 00:26:07.508
A new regiment consisting only of nobles to keep them happy.

00:26:07.568 --> 00:26:13.001
And then the rest of the army made up of my soldiers, the real army.

00:26:13.062 --> 00:26:15.594
Everyone was happy.

00:26:15.654 --> 00:26:21.796
I decided to go on a trip through the kingdom to see the general conditions.

00:26:21.856 --> 00:26:26.134
The king wanted to come too and told me to wait.

00:26:26.194 --> 00:26:28.935
He had to do his ceremony.

00:26:28.995 --> 00:26:32.746
He touched the sick and cured them.

00:26:32.806 --> 00:26:34.877
Often it worked.

00:26:34.937 --> 00:26:40.499
People were convinced his touch was magic and their belief made them better.

00:26:40.559 --> 00:26:42.780
The king did his best.

00:26:42.840 --> 00:26:44.920
He was a good man.

00:26:44.981 --> 00:26:49.494
The ceremony was very long and I was bored.

00:26:49.554 --> 00:26:54.598
He touched every sick person and gave them a coin.

00:26:54.658 --> 00:26:59.830
I decided to stop the gold coins and make copper ones.

00:26:59.890 --> 00:27:03.662
This saved the kingdom a lot of money.

00:27:03.722 --> 00:27:11.056
During the touching ceremony, I saw another of my innovations, a newspaper.

00:27:11.116 --> 00:27:14.162
I was very happy with the result.

00:27:14.222 --> 00:27:22.945
It wasn't perfect, and I wanted to improve it, but it was good enough, and everyone was amazed by it.

00:27:23.005 --> 00:27:28.440
I was as proud of it as a mother of her new baby.

00:27:28.500 --> 00:27:36.076
I suggested the king tell Queen Guinevere of our departure, but he was sad.

00:27:36.136 --> 00:27:43.738
When Sir Lancelot is here, the Queen doesn't notice if I arrive or depart, he said.

00:27:43.798 --> 00:27:46.176
I was sorry for him.

00:27:46.236 --> 00:27:53.701
I thought the queen was beautiful, but not very intelligent.

00:27:53.761 --> 00:28:03.558
Later that evening I helped the king to dress himself as a peasant, ready for our journey into his kingdom.

00:28:03.618 --> 00:28:06.261
I cut his hair short.

00:28:06.321 --> 00:28:14.887
Nobles had long hair cut short at the front, and peasants had short hair, and the slaves had long hair.

00:28:14.947 --> 00:28:21.400
I cut his hair like a peasant and gave him a long, simple tunic.

00:28:21.460 --> 00:28:24.740
We left early in the morning.

00:28:24.800 --> 00:28:28.762
On the road some noble people passed.

00:28:28.822 --> 00:28:32.534
I had to tell the king to bow to them.

00:28:32.594 --> 00:28:35.295
He didn't know how to behave.

00:28:35.355 --> 00:28:40.156
He wasn't good at bowing and one of the nobles tried to hit him.

00:28:40.216 --> 00:28:44.194
I stepped in and he whipped me instead.

00:28:44.254 --> 00:28:47.522
Next, we met two knights.

00:28:47.582 --> 00:28:50.735
The king did not move off the road.

00:28:50.795 --> 00:28:54.898
He didn't understand that peasants had no rights.

00:28:54.958 --> 00:28:58.300
He believed the knights would ride around him.

00:28:58.360 --> 00:29:00.172
They didn't.

00:29:00.232 --> 00:29:03.734
They insulted the king, who answered.

00:29:03.794 --> 00:29:06.746
This made them furious.

00:29:06.806 --> 00:29:11.159
To save the situation, I insulted them more.

00:29:11.219 --> 00:29:18.816
They turned and started to attack us, so I threw some dynamite at them, and they exploded.

00:29:18.876 --> 00:29:21.788
The king thought it was magic.

00:29:21.848 --> 00:29:25.322
I told him I could not repeat it another time.

00:29:25.382 --> 00:29:32.288
He said, You must read my thoughts and stop me before I make mistakes.

00:29:32.348 --> 00:29:35.420
I can't, I answered.

00:29:35.481 --> 00:29:37.672
He was amazed.

00:29:37.732 --> 00:29:42.274
But Merlin can, he said.

00:29:42.334 --> 00:29:45.755
I realized I had made a mistake.

00:29:45.815 --> 00:29:51.486
I said, Merlin can see a few minutes into the future.

00:29:51.546 --> 00:29:55.657
I can see centuries into the future.

00:29:55.717 --> 00:30:00.268
I don't bother with small prophecy like Merlin.

00:30:00.328 --> 00:30:05.721
He was convinced.

00:30:05.781 --> 00:30:12.575
Chapter 4. The Yankee and the King.

00:30:12.635 --> 00:30:21.382
On the morning of the fourth day, when the sun was coming up, I decided to drill the king.

00:30:21.442 --> 00:30:27.816
Sir, I said, you are too like a soldier, a lord.

00:30:27.876 --> 00:30:29.807
This is not good.

00:30:29.867 --> 00:30:33.766
You must try to look poor and miserable.

00:30:33.826 --> 00:30:39.746
The king tried to walk like a poor peasant, but he was not convincing.

00:30:39.807 --> 00:30:42.578
He had too much spirit.

00:30:42.638 --> 00:30:49.824
I said to him, what will you say when we ask for hospitality in a house?

00:30:49.884 --> 00:30:54.459
Varlet, give me what you have, answered the king.

00:30:54.479 --> 00:31:02.131
No, you cannot say, Varlet, you are not a lord, I answered.

00:31:02.191 --> 00:31:05.989
You must say, brother.

00:31:06.049 --> 00:31:09.430
The king tried his best.

00:31:09.490 --> 00:31:12.683
Give me the sack, he said.

00:31:12.743 --> 00:31:17.536
I must try to stoop under weights that are not honorable.

00:31:17.596 --> 00:31:22.688
He tried, but it was very difficult for him to stoop.

00:31:22.749 --> 00:31:25.160
I thought about work.

00:31:25.220 --> 00:31:30.641
I thought about the people who believe that a day of intellectual work is hard.

00:31:30.701 --> 00:31:35.422
They don't understand that work is physical.

00:31:35.482 --> 00:31:42.658
It is silly to pay higher wages to intellectuals than to people who work with their bodies.

00:31:42.718 --> 00:31:47.712
We saw a very small poor house in the distance.

00:31:47.772 --> 00:31:51.274
We arrived in the middle of the afternoon.

00:31:51.334 --> 00:31:53.826
There was no sign of life.

00:31:53.886 --> 00:31:58.564
Everything looked ruined and there was no living thing.

00:31:58.624 --> 00:32:04.410
We pushed the door open and saw some forms in the dark.

00:32:04.470 --> 00:32:06.980
One sat up.

00:32:07.040 --> 00:32:09.441
Have mercy!

00:32:09.501 --> 00:32:11.302
cried a woman.

00:32:11.362 --> 00:32:13.913
They have taken everything.

00:32:13.973 --> 00:32:16.023
There is nothing here.

00:32:16.043 --> 00:32:21.936
I do not want anything, poor woman, I said.

00:32:21.996 --> 00:32:25.796
Then you are not a priest or a lord?

00:32:25.856 --> 00:32:27.518
She asked.

00:32:27.578 --> 00:32:32.802
No, I am a stranger, I replied.

00:32:32.862 --> 00:32:35.344
Let me come in and help you.

00:32:35.404 --> 00:32:39.446
You are sick and in trouble, I said.

00:32:39.506 --> 00:32:42.619
Go away, she said.

00:32:42.679 --> 00:32:48.162
We are in trouble with the lord and the Church, and we have the smallpox.

00:32:48.222 --> 00:32:49.943
You must go away.

00:32:49.963 --> 00:32:57.137
I told the king to go away, but he refused.

00:32:57.197 --> 00:33:03.020
The king does not know fear and has no trouble with the church.

00:33:03.080 --> 00:33:05.471
I must stay and help.

00:33:05.532 --> 00:33:09.935
It is the duty of a knight, he said.

00:33:09.995 --> 00:33:13.357
We gave the woman water.

00:33:13.417 --> 00:33:20.422
Please go out that ladder and tell me what you see, said the woman.

00:33:20.482 --> 00:33:25.739
The king went up the ladder which led to another part of the little hut.

00:33:25.799 --> 00:33:29.684
On his way, he noticed a man.

00:33:29.744 --> 00:33:32.966
Is that your husband sleeping?

00:33:33.026 --> 00:33:34.626
He asked.

00:33:34.686 --> 00:33:36.277
No.

00:33:36.337 --> 00:33:39.298
He died three hours ago.

00:33:39.358 --> 00:33:44.500
Now he is at peace, said the woman.

00:33:44.560 --> 00:33:51.213
The king climbed the ladder and came back with a poor girl of fifteen.

00:33:51.273 --> 00:33:53.464
She was dying.

00:33:53.524 --> 00:33:56.047
He said there was another girl.

00:33:56.107 --> 00:33:58.510
who was already dead.

00:33:58.570 --> 00:34:04.994
He laid the girl next to the woman who sat with her until she died.

00:34:05.054 --> 00:34:09.418
I brought the other child to lie next to her.

00:34:09.478 --> 00:34:13.100
The woman told us her story.

00:34:13.160 --> 00:34:20.356
They were persecuted by the lord and the church who made them work and took all their property.

00:34:20.416 --> 00:34:28.272
they had nothing to eat, and their three sons were unjustly in prison for a theft they had not committed.

00:34:28.332 --> 00:34:31.284
Then they got smallpox.

00:34:31.345 --> 00:34:36.888
At midnight, they were all dead.

00:34:36.948 --> 00:34:43.302
We continued our journey and came to a small house.

00:34:43.362 --> 00:34:48.667
We asked for hospitality, and the couple who lived there was kind.

00:34:48.727 --> 00:34:55.914
I spoke to the man and discovered that he did not like the injustice of the country's laws.

00:34:55.974 --> 00:34:58.247
I liked him.

00:34:58.307 --> 00:35:05.704
We stayed for some days with the man whose name was Marco and his wife Phyllis.

00:35:05.764 --> 00:35:11.228
I said the king was a farmer and I was his assistant.

00:35:11.288 --> 00:35:17.175
One day I decided to have a special lunch at Marco's house.

00:35:17.235 --> 00:35:22.960
I invited a lot of people, all the craftsmen of the town.

00:35:23.020 --> 00:35:28.254
Marco was terrified by the cost, which was too much for him.

00:35:28.314 --> 00:35:30.996
I paid for everything.

00:35:31.056 --> 00:35:34.878
Everyone thought I was very rich.

00:35:34.938 --> 00:35:40.542
At the lunch, I tried to explain economics to the men.

00:35:40.602 --> 00:35:47.546
I told them that in my part of the country, people earned less, but everything cost less.

00:35:47.606 --> 00:35:52.200
So in my part of the country, people were better off.

00:35:52.260 --> 00:35:55.343
They couldn't understand.

00:35:55.403 --> 00:35:58.366
But we earn double what you earn!

00:35:58.426 --> 00:36:00.087
This is better!

00:36:00.148 --> 00:36:02.390
insisted one man.

00:36:02.450 --> 00:36:06.864
But we pay less than half of what you pay.

00:36:06.924 --> 00:36:13.007
Therefore we have more money and can buy more things, I replied.

00:36:13.067 --> 00:36:20.498
They could not understand the idea which was new to them, and I could not explain it to them.

00:36:20.558 --> 00:36:23.529
I was very disappointed.

00:36:23.589 --> 00:36:26.550
So I tried another subject.

00:36:26.610 --> 00:36:35.294
I talked about crime and punishment, and I said they were committing crimes by earning more than was allowed by their Lord.

00:36:35.354 --> 00:36:37.615
This was a mistake.

00:36:37.675 --> 00:36:42.800
I thought we could laugh about it, but they were terrified.

00:36:42.860 --> 00:36:48.277
They didn't know me, and they were worried that I wanted to report them.

00:36:48.337 --> 00:36:54.542
The king started talking about farming, but he knew nothing about it.

00:36:54.602 --> 00:36:58.255
The men started to say that he was mad.

00:36:58.315 --> 00:37:03.439
One wants to betray us, and the other is mad.

00:37:03.499 --> 00:37:07.162
They shouted.

00:37:07.222 --> 00:37:15.218
A fight started and the king was delighted, but I made him escape.

00:37:15.279 --> 00:37:17.110
We were in danger.

00:37:17.170 --> 00:37:24.386
We ran to the woods and hid in a tree, but the people found us and wanted to kill us.

00:37:24.446 --> 00:37:28.890
Luckily a noble arrived and saved us.

00:37:28.950 --> 00:37:34.344
He took us with him to a nearby town where he had business.

00:37:34.404 --> 00:37:37.927
Then we had another terrible surprise.

00:37:37.987 --> 00:37:42.908
He took us to the market and sold us as slaves.

00:37:42.969 --> 00:37:48.120
He sold the king for seven dollars and me for nine.

00:37:48.180 --> 00:37:49.820
I was offended.

00:37:49.880 --> 00:37:54.732
I was worth at least fifteen and the king twelve.

00:37:54.792 --> 00:38:01.074
We were chained to the slaves by the master who was hard and cruel.

00:38:01.134 --> 00:38:05.935
We got lost in the snow and five people died.

00:38:05.995 --> 00:38:11.730
Then a woman arrived screaming and tried to find protection with us.

00:38:11.790 --> 00:38:16.845
The people in her village said she was a witch and wanted to burn her.

00:38:16.905 --> 00:38:20.098
Our slave master helped them.

00:38:20.158 --> 00:38:22.911
We could not help her.

00:38:22.971 --> 00:38:30.756
Our master was angry about the dead slaves and revenged himself on this poor woman.

00:38:30.816 --> 00:38:33.716
Then we saw a procession.

00:38:33.776 --> 00:38:38.420
A young girl of eighteen was sitting on a coffin in a cart.

00:38:38.480 --> 00:38:40.402
She had a baby.

00:38:40.462 --> 00:38:45.145
With her was a priest who told her story.

00:38:45.206 --> 00:38:49.008
She was a young wife and mother.

00:38:49.068 --> 00:38:53.522
Then the army took her husband away to be a soldier.

00:38:53.582 --> 00:38:58.274
She had no work and was starving with her baby.

00:38:58.334 --> 00:39:02.436
so she stole a small piece of linen.

00:39:02.496 --> 00:39:05.849
The judge decided to hang her.

00:39:05.909 --> 00:39:11.334
The owner of the linen felt so bad he committed suicide.

00:39:11.394 --> 00:39:25.752
She cried and held her baby, but the priest, who was very kind to her, made a speech against the laws and the sentence and promised to look after the baby.

00:39:25.812 --> 00:39:35.352
There was gratitude in her face when she died.

00:39:35.412 --> 00:39:41.994
I had a plan to escape.

00:39:42.054 --> 00:39:48.396
I had to wait for many weeks, but in London my chance finally came.

00:39:48.456 --> 00:39:51.677
Immediately things went wrong.

00:39:51.737 --> 00:39:55.079
I couldn't get the king's chains off.

00:39:55.139 --> 00:39:58.371
the slave master interrupted me.

00:39:58.432 --> 00:40:03.634
When he went outside I followed him and attacked him in the dark.

00:40:03.694 --> 00:40:07.585
But the police arrested me and put me in jail.

00:40:07.646 --> 00:40:11.077
I said that I was a noble servant.

00:40:11.137 --> 00:40:15.288
They were afraid of the nobles and let me go.

00:40:15.348 --> 00:40:20.881
Then I discovered that the other slaves had killed the slave master.

00:40:20.941 --> 00:40:25.839
They were all in prison, condemned to death.

00:40:25.899 --> 00:40:31.668
I found a telegraph station and sent a message to Clarence.

00:40:31.728 --> 00:40:35.030
Send knights to save the king and I.

00:40:35.090 --> 00:40:36.781
They want to hang us.

00:40:36.841 --> 00:40:38.962
Tomorrow.

00:40:39.022 --> 00:40:43.014
Everyone in London was looking for me.

00:40:43.074 --> 00:40:47.368
They took the slaves about London to recognize me.

00:40:47.428 --> 00:40:50.389
Unfortunately one of them saw me.

00:40:50.449 --> 00:40:55.927
They took me to the other slaves and decided to hang us that day.

00:40:55.987 --> 00:40:59.724
The knights would never arrive in time.

00:40:59.784 --> 00:41:02.516
It was too late.

00:41:02.576 --> 00:41:06.368
They took us to the execution place.

00:41:06.428 --> 00:41:12.002
The king tried to say who he was, but everyone laughed at him.

00:41:12.062 --> 00:41:15.424
They started to hang the slaves.

00:41:15.484 --> 00:41:19.738
Then they started to put the rope around the king's neck.

00:41:19.798 --> 00:41:21.719
It was dreadful.

00:41:21.779 --> 00:41:24.220
I couldn't move.

00:41:24.280 --> 00:41:26.326
Suddenly.

00:41:26.386 --> 00:41:28.872
a grand sight.

00:41:28.932 --> 00:41:35.277
Five hundred knights in armour, on bicycles.

00:41:35.337 --> 00:41:39.890
Sir Lancelot and the knights saved the king.

00:41:39.950 --> 00:41:43.314
Clarence was very happy.

00:41:43.374 --> 00:41:45.766
What a surprise, eh?

00:41:45.826 --> 00:41:46.836
He said.

00:41:46.896 --> 00:41:50.850
The boy's practiced for a long time.

00:41:50.910 --> 00:41:55.490
Soon I was home again in Camelot.

00:41:55.550 --> 00:41:59.169
I had to fight Sir Sagramor in a tournament.

00:41:59.229 --> 00:42:01.480
Everyone came to see it.

00:42:01.540 --> 00:42:05.452
The knights all supported Sir Sagramor.

00:42:05.512 --> 00:42:09.174
Merlin did some magic to protect him.

00:42:09.234 --> 00:42:14.628
I only had Clarence to support me.

00:42:14.688 --> 00:42:18.540
We started the fight.

00:42:18.600 --> 00:42:24.434
Sir Sagramor was in full armour, but I was wearing light clothes.

00:42:24.494 --> 00:42:30.164
Everyone thought I was ridiculous, but I could move fast and avoid him.

00:42:30.224 --> 00:42:32.594
He couldn't catch me.

00:42:32.654 --> 00:42:36.516
He got very angry and wanted to kill me.

00:42:36.576 --> 00:42:39.466
I used my lasso.

00:42:39.526 --> 00:42:44.307
They didn't know about cowboys and were amazed.

00:42:44.367 --> 00:42:49.578
I pulled Sir Sagramor off his horse and won the fight.

00:42:49.638 --> 00:42:55.720
But Merlin stole my lasso, and Sir Sagramor wanted to fight again.

00:42:55.780 --> 00:42:58.672
I shot him with a gun.

00:42:58.732 --> 00:43:00.652
Everyone was shocked.

00:43:00.712 --> 00:43:02.613
They thought it was magic.

00:43:02.673 --> 00:43:04.984
The knights were angry.

00:43:05.044 --> 00:43:09.066
Five hundred of them attacked me all at once.

00:43:09.126 --> 00:43:13.308
I shot some, and the others escaped.

00:43:13.368 --> 00:43:16.634
Everyone was afraid of me.

00:43:16.694 --> 00:43:20.713
For three years, I improved the country.

00:43:20.773 --> 00:43:25.046
It was happy, civilized, with more money.

00:43:25.107 --> 00:43:27.668
Slavery was illegal.

00:43:27.728 --> 00:43:33.894
I wanted a republic, but decided to wait until King Arthur died.

00:43:33.954 --> 00:43:38.748
Then, one day, my child got sick.

00:43:38.808 --> 00:43:41.450
I was married to Sandy.

00:43:41.510 --> 00:43:44.923
I had married her because it was polite.

00:43:44.983 --> 00:43:48.094
but then I realized I loved her.

00:43:48.154 --> 00:43:51.416
I was totally happy with her.

00:43:51.476 --> 00:43:53.598
We had a daughter.

00:43:53.658 --> 00:43:56.208
Now she was sick.

00:43:56.268 --> 00:44:02.702
Sir Lancelot, a very kind man, helped Sandy and me to look after her.

00:44:02.762 --> 00:44:09.836
Then we decided to take her to the sea for her health and sailed to France.

00:44:09.896 --> 00:44:15.074
When there was no news, I sailed back.

00:44:15.134 --> 00:44:18.000
Everything was a disaster.

00:44:18.060 --> 00:44:28.882
Clarence explained that the king was dead, Guinevere was a nun, the knights were fighting and the church wanted to dominate the land.

00:44:28.942 --> 00:44:33.833
We had to fight, it was time for the revolution.

00:44:33.893 --> 00:44:39.134
We declared a republic and the knights came to fight us.

00:44:39.194 --> 00:44:43.766
We hid in a cave and put dynamite everywhere.

00:44:43.826 --> 00:44:49.880
There were only fifty-four of us, and twenty-five thousand of them.

00:44:49.940 --> 00:44:56.664
But when they attacked, we electrocuted them, and then made them explode.

00:44:56.725 --> 00:44:59.987
We won.

00:45:00.047 --> 00:45:06.852
Postscript by Clarence. I must finish the story.

00:45:06.912 --> 00:45:09.360
The boss made a mistake.

00:45:09.420 --> 00:45:16.968
He wanted to offer help to some injured knights, but one of them recognized him and stabbed him.

00:45:17.028 --> 00:45:22.272
Then we realized that our cook was Merlin in disguise.

00:45:22.332 --> 00:45:28.474
Merlin did some terrible magic, and now the Boss is sleeping.

00:45:28.534 --> 00:45:32.797
He will never wake again.

00:45:32.857 --> 00:45:41.066
Final Postscript by Mark Twain. At dawn, I stopped reading.

00:45:41.126 --> 00:45:45.180
I went to the stranger's room and knocked on the door.

00:45:45.240 --> 00:45:47.601
There was no answer.

00:45:47.662 --> 00:45:50.334
He was delirious.

00:45:50.394 --> 00:45:52.766
He spoke.

00:45:52.826 --> 00:45:56.829
Sandy, is that you?

00:45:56.889 --> 00:46:01.942
At last, now I can go back to you and our daughter.

00:46:02.002 --> 00:46:05.585
It was terrible without you.

00:46:05.646 --> 00:46:09.306
I am in the wrong century.

00:46:09.366 --> 00:46:11.886
A trumpet!

00:46:11.946 --> 00:46:15.412
It is the king!

00:46:15.472 --> 00:46:19.539
He never finished his sentence.